WEBVTT

NOTE Cues sit near the top (line:4%) so they don't cover the film's lower-third captions.

1a-1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.700 line:4% align:center
Here’s a MOSAIC result

1a-2
00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.340 line:4% align:center
for a fictional food business.

1b-1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.154 line:4% align:center
It starts with context:

1b-2
00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:09.356 line:4% align:center
industry, size, markets, buyers and goals.

1b-3
00:00:09.356 --> 00:00:12.330 line:4% align:center
That decides which questions are asked.

2a-1
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.594 line:4% align:center
The owner answers in plain terms:

2a-2
00:00:15.594 --> 00:00:18.320 line:4% align:center
yes or no, or a figure they already know.

3a-1
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.823 line:4% align:center
Results open with two overall scores:

3a-2
00:00:26.823 --> 00:00:29.180 line:4% align:center
raw, and weighted for this industry.

3b-1
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.490 line:4% align:center
Beside them, coverage shows how much was answered.

4a-1
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.270 line:4% align:center
Four category scores show where the business stands.

4b-1
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.461 line:4% align:center
The archetype reads the same answers another way.

4b-2
00:00:39.461 --> 00:00:41.895 line:4% align:center
This business is the Mediator:

4b-3
00:00:41.895 --> 00:00:44.330 line:4% align:center
engagement first, then commitments.

4c-1
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.420 line:4% align:center
“Why this archetype?” shows how it was worked out.

5a-1
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.553 line:4% align:center
Optional AI recommendations then name the gaps

5a-2
00:00:51.553 --> 00:00:52.580 line:4% align:center
worth attention.

5b-1
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.697 line:4% align:center
Each gap lists the references it drew on, so

5b-2
00:00:55.697 --> 00:00:57.400 line:4% align:center
you can check whether it fits.

6a-1
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.978 line:4% align:center
Levers ask “what if?” Change one answer, watch

6a-2
00:01:05.978 --> 00:01:08.180 line:4% align:center
the scores move, then put it back.

6b-1
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.663 line:4% align:center
It doesn't predict costs, savings or

6b-2
00:01:10.663 --> 00:01:11.910 line:4% align:center
real-world results.

7a-1
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.295 line:4% align:center
The report downloads as a web page you

7a-2
00:01:16.295 --> 00:01:17.500 line:4% align:center
can print to PDF.

7b-1
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.920 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC. The pieces that matter.
